## Writing Principles
- Simple, succinct, technical, factual; lead with the answer
- Active voice, present tense, concrete nouns; `eve` lowercase
- Consistent capability names with `ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Follow `.agents/skills/technical-writing/` (verify against this repo)
- 300-500 words/section, remove redundancy; no promotional adjectives

## Content Structure
- Clear title → short intro → H2/H3 → examples → links to hosted Basilic docs where tasks belong there
- One concept per section; happy path before alternatives

## Organization
- DRY: one canonical home per topic across `PRODUCT.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `DESIGN.md`, and READMEs
- Progressive disclosure; do not invent files to fill template slots
- Semantic feature parity with root README (same capabilities, different copy)

## Layers
- Root product markdown owns the Coin Tracker story and boundaries. Visual language is `DESIGN.md`. Hosted technical guides live at https://basilic-docs.vercel.app when `AGENTS.md` says upstream wins
- READMEs are how to run apps and packages; they link out, no duplication of architecture treatises
- Update these files when behavior, architecture, commands, or conventions change
